# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude Code / template-internal
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# User-specific Claude Code permissions (never shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Developer Learning Mode runtime state — private by default (see below for opt-in).
# Knowledge files contain a learner's mistakes, prior understanding, and revision
# history. That is private learning material by default. config.json stores per-
# developer level/focus preferences and stays private even when knowledge is shared.
.claude/learn/knowledge/
.claude/learn/config.json

# ── Optional: opt-in to a shared team knowledge base ─────────────────────────
# If your team wants a shared, domain-organized knowledge base that accumulates
# across everyone's sessions, REMOVE the `.claude/learn/knowledge/` line above
# AND uncomment the two inversion lines below. The config.json line stays as-is
# (level and focus are per-developer preferences, not team state).
#
# !.claude/learn/knowledge/
# !.claude/learn/knowledge/**
#
# Considerations before opting in:
#   - Knowledge files will contain revision history ("Superseded 2026-05-14: ...")
#     visible to the team.
#   - A junior's foundational entries and a senior's trade-off entries will
#     coexist. That is the point of the layered knowledge base, but the team
#     should be ready for it.
#   - Knowledge files reveal the team's mistakes over time. Psychological safety
#     matters.
# See ADR-027 for the design rationale of integrating this opt-in block into
# .gitignore (it lived in a separate .gitignore.example file before 2026-05-21).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editors / IDEs
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.history/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment & secrets (never commit)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Private keys & certificates
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519

# Tool credentials
.npmrc
.netrc
.pypirc

# Cloud provider credentials
.aws/credentials
service-account*.json
gcp-credentials*.json

# Generic credential files (rename if a real artifact happens to match)
credentials.json
secrets.yml
secrets.yaml

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logs & temporary files
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
tmp/
.cache/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Language / framework ignores
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Extend this section for your stack. Recommended references:
#   https://github.com/github/gitignore
#
# Node.js / TypeScript:
#   node_modules/
#   dist/
#   build/
#   coverage/
#
# Python:
#   __pycache__/
#   *.pyc
#   .venv/
#   .pytest_cache/
#   .mypy_cache/
#
# Go:
#   vendor/
#   *.test
#   *.out
#
# Rust:
#   target/
#
# Java / Kotlin:
#   .gradle/
#   build/
#   *.class
